WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:04.130
Please welcome from our L.A. studio Max Greenfield.

2
00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:09.130
(upbeat music)
(audience applauding)

3
00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:10.433
Hi!

4
00:00:11.584 --> 00:00:12.960
Hi, Max.

5
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.273
How are you?
I'm so good, how are you?

6
00:00:17.141 --> 00:00:19.210
I'm doing well.

7
00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:20.120
I like what you're wearing,

8
00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.645
it's a very Annie Hall vibe, it's great.

9
00:00:22.645 --> 00:00:25.600
Oh, she's a bit of my style icon,

10
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.277
so thank you so much.

11
00:00:27.277 --> 00:00:31.040
Well, me too, she's my style icon as well.

12
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:34.190
Hair/makeup/wardrobe is a very important step

13
00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:36.820
when you're playing a part.

14
00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:37.830
I agree.

15
00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.610
When you get really good people who are doing it

16
00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:41.680
all of a sudden you realize when you get on stage

17
00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:42.910
and you look at yourself in the camera,

18
00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:44.110
you're a totally different person

19
00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.580
and then everything else is easy.

20
00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:47.800
Well, it's a funny segue,

21
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.130
but one of the reasons I had brought that up

22
00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.070
is because I was watching,

23
00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:55.720
while I was looking at pictures of you and your daughter,

24
00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:59.140
she had done a rainbow eye on you.

25
00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:03.080
And it's funny 'cause my daughter Olive, who's eight,

26
00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:06.330
just did a rainbow eye on herself

27
00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:08.140
and it just looked so cool.

28
00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:11.860
And I love that you're the kind of dad

29
00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:14.693
that will let your daughter do makeup on you.

30
00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:17.820
She loves makeup.

31
00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:20.525
It's Beauty Week on the show this week, right?

32
00:01:20.525 --> 00:01:21.358
Is it!

33
00:01:21.358 --> 00:01:23.290
In fact, you're really kicking it off.

34
00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:25.063
Oh, well this is exciting.

35
00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:27.380
I know they they showed me

36
00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:30.540
a bunch of stuff we have over here.

37
00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:32.850
I thought you could walk me through some of the products

38
00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:34.490
and we could,

39
00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:35.900
we could apply some makeup.

40
00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:38.330
I would love it!

41
00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:40.110
Drew, what am I putting on first?

42
00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:43.270
Why don't we start with the eyes?

43
00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:44.200
And by the way,

44
00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.390
this is all actually for your daughter.

45
00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:50.860
So I'm gonna send you a fresh kit for her

46
00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:52.760
so that it's all brand new and perfect.

47
00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:55.310
I'll have that to you later today.

48
00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:57.080
By the way, this stuff looks so nice.

49
00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:58.570
The packaging's very nice.

50
00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:00.720
I don't know what any of it is but it looks great.

51
00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.150
Thank you, Max.

52
00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:03.700
We make all the packaging.

53
00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:06.840
I've been doing this business for nearly a decade.

54
00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:09.390
You know what, I'm just gonna have you do it with a finger.

55
00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:10.223
Yeah.

56
00:02:10.223 --> 00:02:12.610
There's a famous makeup artist named Pat McGrath

57
00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:14.200
and she does everything with her finger.

58
00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.450
Sure, I love Pat.

59
00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:18.800
Dig your finger in relatively strongly

60
00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.590
and then just go right on your eyelids.

61
00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:23.072
No, I knew that.

62
00:02:23.072 --> 00:02:25.540
(audience laughing)

63
00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:28.100
Uh huh, okay, now I want you go

64
00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:31.380
like it's a deodorant on your cheekbones.

65
00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.910
Now we're talking.

66
00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:34.370
Yeah, good, perfect.

67
00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:37.170
Now I'm gonna move on to lips.

68
00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:42.170
Find where your middle point is and then work left or right.

69
00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:47.970
Uh huh. (laughing)
(audience laughing)

70
00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:51.790
Yes!
(audience cheering)

71
00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:54.180
Max, how do you like making "The Neighborhood"?

72
00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:55.780
It's such a,

73
00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:59.297
a powerful, amazing show

74
00:03:01.451 --> 00:03:06.030
in its format, in its tone,

75
00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:08.970
thematically the storyline--

76
00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:11.663
Well, we have a really wonderful group of writers.

77
00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:13.733
I know, let me,

78
00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:16.410
let's address this.

79
00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:19.459
Maybe we should have done this question first.

80
00:03:19.459 --> 00:03:22.891
I'm literally thinking the same thing.

81
00:03:22.891 --> 00:03:25.370
(audience laughing)

82
00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:26.750
We're just really happy to be back

83
00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:27.950
for a season (giggling).

84
00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:33.120
You really like rolled through the question,

85
00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:34.913
then I go, oh, okay, we're going.

86
00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:39.370
And then I could just disregard what's happening

87
00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:42.205
which may have been the move.

88
00:03:42.205 --> 00:03:45.415
Okay, I'm gonna switch questions.

89
00:03:45.415 --> 00:03:48.260
I will simply answer it with this.

90
00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:52.980
We have an incredible, incredible group of people

91
00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:54.860
on that show.

92
00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:56.780
From Jim Reynolds who created the show

93
00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:58.770
who was on "Big Bang Theory" forever,

94
00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:01.250
Cedric the Entertainer who really

95
00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:04.980
is so much more than just an actor on the show.

96
00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:08.410
He's a producer on the show and really crafts every story

97
00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:10.060
and makes sure that the Butler family

98
00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:13.535
is represented in an organic, authentic way.

99
00:04:13.535 --> 00:04:16.740
Tichina Arnold who has been on TV forever and is probably

100
00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:19.683
the most talented sitcom actress I've ever worked with.

101
00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:22.630
Everyone on the show from top to bottom.

102
00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:25.130
Beth Behrs who plays my wife who I love.

103
00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:26.970
Marcel Spears, Sheaun McKinney,

104
00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:29.070
it's just a great, great group.

105
00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:30.980
Max, may I ask,

106
00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:34.680
how do you feel when your daughter is doing makeup on you?

107
00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:36.840
What goes through your mind?

108
00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:38.670
She's gotten really good at makeup.

109
00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:39.990
She'll come out,

110
00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:42.590
she'll do it in the morning where she has a half hour

111
00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:44.940
between breakfast and her Zoom school,

112
00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:46.427
and then she'll be like

113
00:04:46.427 --> 00:04:48.430
"Check out what I just did."

114
00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:49.263
And we'll go,

115
00:04:49.263 --> 00:04:52.627
"You can't be on your Zoom for school

116
00:04:52.627 --> 00:04:54.627
"with a full face of makeup.

117
00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:55.707
"Having said that,

118
00:04:55.707 --> 00:04:58.173
"you did a really good job and we're very proud of you.

119
00:04:58.173 --> 00:05:00.970
"But you need to take it off."

120
00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:05.730
Seems like you're exactly what a female needs.

121
00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:08.650
You're fun, you're empowering,
(Max laughing)

122
00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:11.890
your humorous, you're playful.

123
00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:14.396
You really are the complete package and--

124
00:05:14.396 --> 00:05:17.453
Yeah, my wife, my wife's somewhere just going like this.

125
00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:22.908
How did you guys meet, may I ask?

126
00:05:22.908 --> 00:05:24.500
We, god almighty,

127
00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:26.610
we met in 2003

128
00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:32.436
and it was just like out at a club.

129
00:05:32.436 --> 00:05:34.070
I love it!

130
00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:36.270
Yeah, well I usually was never allowed

131
00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.030
into those clubs or bars,

132
00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:40.080
and I finally got into one and I was like

133
00:05:41.167 --> 00:05:43.840
"I got to find something in here."

134
00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:44.970
But also, Max,

135
00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:49.350
I think you're gonna give a little delusion to women

136
00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:51.220
that they think if they're gonna go to a club

137
00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:52.630
and meet a man like you,

138
00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:55.090
I think you're gonna give women a lot of hope.

139
00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:56.240
No, no, no, no, no.

140
00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:58.150
One, you're me too much credit,

141
00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:02.797
and two, I've met a woman who has just really,

142
00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:06.920
through many different techniques,

143
00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:09.580
changed me in a lot of different ways.

144
00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:10.540
Well, Max,

145
00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:13.920
I am just thrilled to be hanging out with you today.

146
00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:18.440
What a great way to kick off this week with a man who is fun

147
00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:20.650
and good to the women in his life.

148
00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:22.980
I think that is important for Beauty Week.

149
00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:26.270
Well, I appreciate it and I'm so happy to be here

150
00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:28.210
and to meet and sit with you

151
00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:30.780
and this has really been special and great.

152
00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:32.490
And obviously rewarding.

153
00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:35.100
Thank you, Max Greenfield.

154
00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:39.230
The season premiere of "The Neighborhood" is tonight on CBS

155
00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:43.080
and airs Mondays eight/seven central.

156
00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:46.280
Thank you, Max, again, so much for being here.

157
00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:48.863 line:15%
(upbeat music)

